From: vivarium <https://github.com/Lillecarl/vivarium>
Subject: [PATCH] um: don't dereference vector queues in get_ringparam when down

The vector driver's rx_queue and tx_queue exist only while the interface
is up: vector_net_open() creates them and vector_net_close() destroys
them. vector_get_ringparam() read vp->rx_queue->max_depth unconditionally,
so `ethtool <iface>` on a down vec interface dereferenced a NULL pointer
(a device never opened, whose private area alloc_etherdev() zeroed) and
panicked the guest:

  Kernel panic - not syncing: Kernel mode fault at addr 0x24
  Comm: ethtool
  rings_prepare_data+0x83 -> vector_get_ringparam

VyOS hits this during boot: it runs ethtool on each configured interface
before bringing it up, which crashed every UML guest that gave a VyOS
node a real segment interface.

Report the configured queue depth (get_depth) when a queue is down; it is
the depth the queue takes when open, so the value is right rather than
merely safe. Also NULL the queue pointers after destroy_queue() in close,
so ethtool on an interface that was up and then taken down reads NULL
rather than a freed queue.

--- a/arch/um/drivers/vector_kern.c
+++ b/arch/um/drivers/vector_kern.c
@@ -1152,10 +1152,14 @@
 	kfree(vp->transport_data);
 	kfree(vp->header_rxbuffer);
 	kfree(vp->header_txbuffer);
-	if (vp->rx_queue != NULL)
+	if (vp->rx_queue != NULL) {
 		destroy_queue(vp->rx_queue);
-	if (vp->tx_queue != NULL)
+		vp->rx_queue = NULL;
+	}
+	if (vp->tx_queue != NULL) {
 		destroy_queue(vp->tx_queue);
+		vp->tx_queue = NULL;
+	}
 	kfree(vp->fds);
 	vp->fds = NULL;
 	vp->in_error = false;
@@ -1428,11 +1432,19 @@
 				 struct netlink_ext_ack *extack)
 {
 	struct vector_private *vp = netdev_priv(netdev);
+	int depth = get_depth(vp->parsed);
 
-	ring->rx_max_pending = vp->rx_queue->max_depth;
-	ring->tx_max_pending = vp->tx_queue->max_depth;
-	ring->rx_pending = vp->rx_queue->max_depth;
-	ring->tx_pending = vp->tx_queue->max_depth;
+	/*
+	 * The queues exist only while the interface is up: they are
+	 * created in vector_net_open() and torn down in vector_net_close().
+	 * ethtool on a down interface would otherwise dereference a NULL
+	 * (never opened) or freed (closed) queue and fault. Report the
+	 * configured depth, which is what the queue holds when open.
+	 */
+	ring->rx_max_pending = vp->rx_queue ? vp->rx_queue->max_depth : depth;
+	ring->tx_max_pending = vp->tx_queue ? vp->tx_queue->max_depth : depth;
+	ring->rx_pending = ring->rx_max_pending;
+	ring->tx_pending = ring->tx_max_pending;
 }
 
 static void vector_get_strings(struct net_device *dev, u32 stringset, u8 *buf)
